# Long-cloth waist pilot — not accepted for publication

Current source/body baseline: main `37fdbf8f`. The private diagnostic fits only the top of the Friar and Shawl skirts to the actual exported coat waist. The underlying coat, skin, skeleton, animations, materials, hem and all stored morph targets stay unchanged.

## Result

**The waist attachment improves, but the complete result is rejected.** Both large open skirt rims are reduced in pickup. The Friar's unchanged rope now clearly floats above the back as a separate ring. Both skirts still have stiff fan-shaped lower folds. This is a useful seam diagnosis, not a finished cloth correction.

